From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:39:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] service: answer a held Connect when the retry after input
 fails

A user Connect on a WiFi network without a stored passphrase is held in
service->pending while the agent is asked for one. When the agent
answers, request_input_cb() starts the connection again with
__connman_service_connect() and drops what it returns. If that call
fails at once - the service is already connecting or connected, IPv4
and IPv6 are both switched off, the agent has to be asked again and
none is left, and so on - nothing answers the held Connect: no attempt
is running, so neither a state change nor the connect timeout comes,
and Disconnect finds nothing to disconnect. Every later Connect on the
service is then refused with InProgress until connmand restarts.
report_error_cb() drops the result of an agent-requested retry in the
same way.

Answer the held Connect with the error in both places, as
connect_service() already does for the first attempt.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/service.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/service.c b/src/service.c
index 41f2a2e..617653d 100644
--- a/src/service.c
+++ b/src/service.c
@@ -9042,10 +9042,14 @@ static void report_error_cb(void *user_context, bool retry,
 {
 	struct connman_service *service = user_context;
 
-	if (retry)
-		__connman_service_connect(service,
+	if (retry) {
+		int err = __connman_service_connect(service,
 					CONNMAN_SERVICE_CONNECT_REASON_USER);
-	else {
+
+		/* See request_input_cb(): answer a retry that did not start. */
+		if (err != -EINPROGRESS)
+			reply_pending(service, -err);
+	} else {
 		/* It is not relevant to stay on Failure state
 		 * when failing is due to wrong user input */
 		__connman_service_clear_error(service);
@@ -9169,9 +9173,18 @@ static void request_input_cb(struct connman_service *service,
 		/* We forget any previous error. */
 		clear_error(service);
 
-		__connman_service_connect(service,
+		err = __connman_service_connect(service,
 					CONNMAN_SERVICE_CONNECT_REASON_USER);
 
+		/*
+		 * The Connect that asked for the input is still waiting. If
+		 * the attempt did not start, answer it now, as
+		 * connect_service() does: nothing else will, and until it is
+		 * answered every Connect on this service gets InProgress.
+		 */
+		if (err != -EINPROGRESS)
+			reply_pending(service, -err);
+
 	} else if (err == -ENOKEY) {
 		__connman_service_indicate_error(service,
 					CONNMAN_SERVICE_ERROR_INVALID_KEY);
